description:
Implement trade/strategy performance attribution and stable CSV/JSON export. These are read-only computations over persisted projections, scoped to one account or scenario.

Before editing, inspect: the persistence read projections from earlier phases for position cycles, orders, fills, signals, evaluations (including NO_SIGNAL and rejection reasons), trailing/protective stop updates, entry-cap/loss-lockout/cooldown decisions and reconciliation drift events; the strategy registry and strategy pair definitions (including vwap_reference); the domain Decimal money/quantity types; the mode/account/scenario identifiers; the clock port and America/New_York session calendar; and any existing mike_trade/reporting modules. Do not import mike_trade/reporting/fees.py or accounting.py; that work runs concurrently in task s.1. Read fee amounts and fee status from persisted fill/fee data as plain strings. Treat the values 'CONFIRMED', 'ESTIMATED' and 'UNAVAILABLE' as the contract, and treat a missing status as 'UNAVAILABLE'.

Implement mike_trade/reporting/metrics.py:
(1) A TradeCycleRecord built per completed or open managed position cycle. It holds:
- account/scenario and symbol;
- originating BUY strategy and SELL strategy, or exit cause when the exit was not a strategy exit (PROTECTIVE_STOP, TRAILING_STOP, MANUAL_CLOSE, FLATTEN, END_OF_DAY, SAFETY);
- strategy pair;
- entry and exit fill-weighted average prices and actual filled quantity, correct under broker partial fills;
- gross P&L, fees by status, net P&L and fees_complete;
- holding duration;
- execution latency (signal to submit to first fill to final fill);
- slippage vs. the signal reference price, in Decimal dollars and basis points;
- trailing-stop update count and last confirmed stop.
(2) Aggregations filterable by account/scenario (required), period (day/week/lifetime and explicit since/until), symbol, BUY strategy, SELL strategy, pair, and exit cause. They produce: trade count, wins/losses, win rate, average win/loss, profit factor, expectancy, total gross/net, average holding duration, and latency/slippage summaries, all in Decimal.
(3) Signal/evaluation outcome counts, rejection reason counts, and entry-cap/loss-lockout/cooldown decision counts with the same filters.
(4) A live-vs-shadow comparison between two explicitly named accounts/scenarios. It aligns trades by symbol, strategy pair and signal bar timestamp, then reports matched trades with fill price/P&L differences, plus missed and extra trades. It never sums balances across the two sides.
(5) Every report carries sample size, a period label and a fixed 'performance_disclaimer' field stating that results are historical/simulated and do not establish profitability.

Implement mike_trade/reporting/export.py:
- Stable versioned CSV and JSON export of report rows, with schema_version, a fixed documented column order per report type, and deterministic row sorting.
- Decimal values serialized as strings with no float conversion, and timestamps as UTC ISO-8601.
- Account identifiers masked; no secrets or raw provider payloads.
- Atomic file writes (temp file plus rename) to an operator-specified path, refusing to overwrite an existing file unless overwrite=True.
- A to_stdout option.
- The supported report types: cycles, strategy summary, pair summary, symbol summary, signals/evaluations, rejections, trailing updates, eligibility decisions, reconciliation drift, and comparison.

Write tests/unit/test_strategy_reports.py with a temporary migrated SQLite DB seeded through existing persistence writers, or with in-memory projection fixtures. Cover:
- partial-fill-weighted P&L;
- protective-stop exit attribution with BUY strategy preserved;
- pair aggregation;
- slippage/latency math;
- missing fee status giving fees_complete=false;
- filter correctness;
- comparison missed/extra trade detection;
- byte-identical CSV and JSON output for identical input;
- Decimal-as-string serialization;
- overwrite refusal;
- account masking.
